#: view/spam-guard/module/statistics.phtml:52
msgid "Submissions"
msgstr ""

#: view/spam-guard/module/statistics.phtml:69
msgid ""
"A weak reason alone is a hint only: two of them are needed to make a spam. "
"Many false positives on a reason mean that its threshold is too strict; many "
"missed spams mean that a check is disabled or that its list is incomplete."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:50
msgid ""
"The spam keywords are now editable in the configuration form of the module. "
"{count} keywords were imported from the files of the modules SpamGuard and "
"Common, that are no longer read."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:65
msgid ""
"A new strategy marks as spam the messages containing a link to a top level "
"domain abused by spammers ({tlds}). The list can be adapted in the config "
"form."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:76
msgid ""
"A new strategy, disabled by default, marks as spam a message sent from an ip "
"that sent a spam detected by a reliable check in any module during the last "
"hours. Before enabling it, add the networks of your institution to the "
"trusted ips in the config form, since its visitors may share a few public "
"ips."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:93
msgid ""
"The dnsbl zone \"zen.spamhaus.org\" was replaced by \"sbl-"
"xbl.spamhaus.org\": \"zen\" includes the policy block list, that lists the "
"consumer access ranges and flags legitimate visitors. Its answers are "
"ignored anyway."
msgstr ""

#: data/scripts/upgrade.php:109
msgid ""
"A new strategy marks as spam the submissions of an ip beyond a number in a "
"few minutes, in any module and whatever the session. The thresholds are in "
"the config form, where the networks of the institution can be listed as "
"trusted ips."
msgstr ""

#: src/SpamStrategy/Dnsbl.php:64
msgid ""
"SpamGuard: the dnsbl zone {zone} refuses the queries sent through a public "
"dns resolver, so the check is inoperative. Use the resolver of the provider "
"or a Spamhaus data query service key."
msgstr ""

