msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:82
msgid ""
"Number of leading hex zeros required on the hash (sha256). The higher the "
"value, the more expensive the client-side computation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:94
msgid "Spam keywords"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:95
msgid ""
"One per line. A message whose subject or body contains one of them, as a "
"whole word, is a spam. This list replaces the one of the module Common, that "
"is no longer read. Check that a keyword is not a legitimate word of your "
"collections before adding it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:106
msgid "Abused top level domains"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:107
msgid ""
"One per line, without dot. A message containing a link to a domain ending "
"with one of them is a spam. The bots rotate their domains every few hours, "
"but stay on a few cheap top level domains."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:118
msgid "DNSBL zones"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:119
msgid ""
"One per line, like sbl-xbl.spamhaus.org. For the zones of Spamhaus, the "
"answers of the policy block list (consumer access ranges, included in "
"zen.spamhaus.org) are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:130
msgid "Maximum number of submissions from the same ip"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:131
msgid ""
"Counted in the journal for all the modules, whatever the session, during the "
"number of minutes below. Keep it high: the visitors of an institution may "
"share a few public ips."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:143
msgid "Minutes during which the submissions of an ip are counted"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:155
msgid "Hours during which an ip that sent a spam is blocked"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:156
msgid ""
"A message sent from an ip that sent a spam in any module during this number "
"of hours is a spam too. Only the spams detected by reliable checks count "
"(honeypot, keyword, link, dnsbl, banned ip, admin), not the ones based on "
"timing. Keep it short: many visitors may share the same ip."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:168
msgid "Trusted ips, never blocked by the reputation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:169
msgid ""
"One ip or range (cidr) by line, for example the networks of the institution, "
"whose visitors share a few public ips."
msgstr ""

#: src/Form/ConfigForm.php:182
msgid "One per line, CIDR accepted."
msgstr ""
